WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:05.480
Yoshino
Tournament

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.480
This is unusual. The finalists are
 the same age and from the same society?

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.480
Class A Final

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.390
And in Class A?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.320
Mashima Taichi 
(Shiranami Society)

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.320
Ayase Chihaya 
(Shiranami Society)

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.140
Chihaya-chan!

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.150
Mashima...

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.820
<i>And in the Class B final...</i>

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:19.830
<b>Retro Go!  Class A</b>

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.700
Kinashi Hiro 
(Hokuo Karuta Society)

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.690
<i>Kinashi Hiro!</i>

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.000
<b>Arashi</b>

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.000
Kotokuji Saneatsu 
(Yokohama 
Arashi Society)

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.000
<i>Kotokuji Saneatsu!</i>

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.040
<i>Age 38, just married.</i>

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.270
<i>My new wife dragged me into karuta,</i>

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.330
<i>so I busted my butt to get 
good enough to impress her!</i>

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.690
<i>I'm the up-and-coming devoted husband 
who picked up this game in no time!</i>

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.970
Class C

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.760
You can do it!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.720
You could never understand what 
I've got riding on this, boy.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.850
You don't have much riding on this at all!

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.450
What about my ten years of karuta experience 
and the expectations of my club?!

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.970
Ten years, and you're still in Class B?
What a side character!

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.300
Make way for the star!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.020
You may begin placing your 
cards in ten minutes.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.200
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.030
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:08.020
Verse 6

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:08.020
Tatsuta
River
Ablaze

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.290
<i>Prez...</i>

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:24.840
Let's take a short break. 
I'll fix your kimono.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.170
Chihaya-chan, Kanade took 
care of you, right?

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.760
This makes it even.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.030
<i>The final...</i>

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.910
<i>I'm playing Taichi in an official match.</i>

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:46.350
Chihaya.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.300
Arata...

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.010
Time for the final, eh?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.460
But I came here with my society by car,

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.270
so I have to leave now.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.350
What?!

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:03.580
I'm dying to stay and watch, but we need to
get our middle schooler members home.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:06.850
Oh... Okay.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.060
Okay. Take care.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:12.510
Uh-huh.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.340
No...

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.300
I'll stay!

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.580
I'll watch the final!

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.060
Even if it's just me, I can kill time 
until the first train in the morning!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.050
I can go to school half a day late.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.850
But...

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.050
I'll watch.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.430
Something tells me I need to watch this.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.850
Don't be such a stranger, Glasses!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.190
You're welcome to spend 
the night at my place!

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.430
We'll play a practice match or two,
and it'll be morning before you know it.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.150
No intention of
letting him sleep

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.190
No, no, Harada-san.
 There's no need for that.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.900
Our president and I will stay, too.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.820
You should leave, Murao-kun. 
You have work tomorrow, don't you?

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.480
If we leave right after the final,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.760
we can get to Fukui by 3 AM.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.590
Won't that be rough on you?

00:03:55.590 --> 00:04:00.080
It'd be rougher on me to leave without 
understanding why I lost to Mashima-kun!

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:05.950
<i>Murao-san...</i>

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.140
You said you were going to win
all your games today in that kimono, right?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.790
I'm going to watch.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.150
I appreciate this, Oe-san.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.370
You always do so much for us.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.550
Just call me Rieko, and we'll call it even.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.230
You're hunching over.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.780
Your back is bent.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.020
O-Oh...

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.710
The collar won't sit right
if your shoulders are too tight.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.910
Uh... Sorry.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.360
Everyone does that when 
they're not used to it.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.220
It's just what happens when 
you live in Western clothes.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.370
Once you get used to wearing a kimono,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.770
the positions of your shoulder 
blades start to change.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:11.200
It makes your shoulders drop backward a bit.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.960
It loosens up your body.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.120
But some parts still need to be tight!

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.640
Did you know this about the obi?

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.850
An obi has several lines drawn across it.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.370
The two lines near the edge of the lappet
 are called the kaikiri-sen.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.360
The kaikiri-sen where 
you make the first fold

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.290
are the two hand-claps given 
when visiting a shrine.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.490
The kasumi-sen is the shrine gate.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.270
The patterned part is
the road leading to the shrine.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.900
And finally, the tesaki 
is the bow after praying.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.910
It will support you.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.430
What do you want to do?

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.660
If we watch the final, we'll get home late.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.280
I want... to stay and watch.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.920
Th-Then I guess I'll have to stay, too.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.160
I'll stay too!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.950
You can go, Cheers!

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:37.430
<i>I've seen Ayase-senpai and Mashima-senpai 
play each other lots of times.</i>

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.940
<i>Every day, in that room...</i>

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.180
<i>I've grown accustomed to it.</i>

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.470
<i>And yet...</i>

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.530
<i>Why...</i>

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.250
<i>...does it feel like I'm seeing 
it for the first time?</i>

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.780
Please place your cards.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.660
<i>Ayase has the advantage.</i>

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.980
<i>Since she won her last match 
by default, she got to rest.</i>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.370
<i>But Mashima's at his peak of exhaustion.</i>

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.180
<i>In all of my data from
the past year and a half,</i>

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.440
<i>Ayase's win rate is 75 percent.</i>

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.770
<i>And it was actually more than 80 percent
before she injured her right hand.</i>

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.260
<i>But...</i>

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.350
<i>Since her injury healed,</i>

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.600
<i>she's won 60 percent
and Mashima has won 40 percent.</i>

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.510
<i>Mashima's improving at
a faster rate than Ayase.</i>

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:57.900
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.410
<i>That's...</i>

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.570
<i>He changed his placement a lot!</i>

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:02.670
<i>Mashima?!</i>

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:13.460
<i>F-Fourteen cards in his top row?</i>

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.130
<i>I've never seen that before!</i>

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:18.880
<i>The one-syllable cards he usually puts 
at the lower right are at the top left?</i>

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.560
<i>All the "May" cards are on the lower right?</i>

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.300
<i>Why? He never puts the ones with 
similar sounds near each other!</i>

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:28.820
<i>Messing with your own placement 
is suicide, Eyelashes.</i>

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.310
<i>This is different from usual.</i>

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.820
<i>He's even ignoring established practice.</i>

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.040
<i>No.</i>

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.780
<i>It's because these two practice 
together as often as they do</i>

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.080
<i>that this change can prove
to be a killer blow.</i>

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.590
<i>To make it harder...</i>

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.700
<i>To make it harder...</i>

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.080
<i>To make it harder...</i>

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:54.080
<i>He came up with this placement
to use against me, and me alone.</i>

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:59.800
This fall, I'm gonna beat you playing 
right-handed in an official match.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.610
<i>It's blowing this way...</i>

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.090
<i>I'm going to beat Chihaya.</i>

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.860
<i>H-He's fired up...</i>

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:15.360
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.590
<i>Chihaya-chan's under pressure.</i>

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:18.000
<i>His little trick blindsided her
and threw her off-pace.</i>

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:26.790
<i>Gust of wind leaves fall leaves falling,</i>

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.490
<i>Sh-She's fast!</i>

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.310
<i>She's still calm! She got 
the "Gust" on her own side!</i>

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.510
<i>Mashima's been fast lately too,</i>

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.490
<i>but she's relaxed and taking 
cards her usual way.</i>

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.130
<i>Don't get too worked up, Mashima!</i>

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.250
<i>May it be that I find...</i>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:46.300
<i>Long last we meet, only for 
me to leave hurriedly,</i>

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.640
<i>for I could not recognize you, like 
the moon hidden behind the clouds</i>

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.310
<i>A one-syllable card from his own side!</i>

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.440
<i>He took it by swiping the whole row!</i>

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.190
<i>"Long"... A one-syllable card
on his own side.</i>

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.680
<i>He's looked at them closely.</i>

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.430
<i>He's given them plenty of thought.</i>

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.370
<i>Eyelashes...</i>

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:07.830
<i>"Impassioned was" and "Impassioned 
vows" are at the center right.</i>

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.050
<i>I know she'll be coming 
after "Impassionate."</i>

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.710
<i>May the time</i>

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.710
<i>May the scarlet</i>

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.710
<i>May my sighs</i>

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.710
<i>May I see</i>

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.500
<i>While she's targeting that area,</i>

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.410
<i>she won't go for the "May" or 
"My" cards, or the top row.</i>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>My own home</i>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>My fear is not</i>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>My life</i>

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.380
<i>He predicted which cards she'd go for</i>

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.850
<i>and placed the key cards 
some distance apart.</i>

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.550
<i>When did Eyelashes learn this?</i>

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.530
<i>I split up the other loaded syllables, too.</i>

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:30.300
<i>You're afraid of committing 
faults, aren't you?</i>

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:37.240
<i>While some dodge the famous waves of 
Takashi shore to avoid getting wet,</i>

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.060
<i>That was a decisive strike!</i>

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.750
<i>She took "While some" that quickly?</i>

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:41.480
<i>She's gotten even better 
at telling sounds apart.</i>

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.630
<i>"While some," "While the," 
"While autumn," "While I,"</i>

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:49.040
<i>"While it brings," "While it 
pains," and "While it may"...</i>

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.890
<i>The "While" cards are tough, but...</i>

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.640
<i>I think I'm close to figuring them out.</i>

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.210
<i>I feel like I was given some kind of hint.</i>

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.520
<i>Taichi's placement is hard to work with,</i>

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:11.550
<i>I deflect your artful words 
to keep my sleeves dry</i>

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.190
<i>but I just need to play my own karuta.</i>

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:19.190
<i>As the years pass, I will 
find myself longing fo</i>

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.240
<i>He took it after covering it.</i>

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.210
<i>His motions are smoother... and faster.</i>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:26.590
<i>Since the dew atop the blades of grass 
has been scattered by the winds,</i>

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:23.540
<i>She took the exact card she was aiming for.</i>

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:24.690
<i>And she's fast!</i>

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:45.760
<i>Even after an injury, 
getting stuck in a rut,</i>

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.800
<i>and failing by getting too worked up...</i>

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:51.740
<i>The Prez and Captain kept going 
through things like that, and yet...</i>

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.030
Ta...

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.310
Tasuki!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.200
E-Excuse us for a moment!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.910
Why did you forget that, Chihaya?!

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:15.810
If you'd had yours on, 
I would've remembered!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.670
You're blaming me?!

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:22.940
<i>The Yoshino Tournament Class A final...</i>

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:25.770
Okay.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:29.550
<i>That's where we are, together.</i>

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.440
<i>Together.</i>

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.940
<i>The sun's gone down, but no one's leaving.</i>

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.560
<i>I have to see this through 
with my own karuta!</i>

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.500
<i>What's going on with this match?</i>

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.280
<i>A match between high schoolers, 
in the same society at that,</i>

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.990
<i>shouldn't feel as tense as a 
typical match, but this...</i>

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:11.290
<i>It's like when those two played in the final 
at the High School Class A Championship.</i>

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.620
<i>Their seriousness wells up,
and they wring out every last drop.</i>

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:29.370
<i>The night breaks to day, 
and day turns to night,</i>

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.290
<i>It's hard to take anything!</i>

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.710
<i>He's able to take cards in that 
long top row with thrusts!</i>

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:36.450
<i>His placement is so unusual, 
it's making Ayase cautious.</i>

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:40.160
<i>But this is important.
Mashima hasn't made any mistakes yet.</i>

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:42.710
<i>But how's he doing it?</i>

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:46.150
<i>It's his seventh match,
so he should be exhausted,</i>

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.750
<i>and he's always had trouble 
forgetting his previous matches...</i>

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:55.810
<i>I forget the initial layout 
and memorize the current one.</i>

00:13:56.590 --> 00:13:59.510
<i>That's not as easy as he made it sound.</i>

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:01.560
<i>But...</i>

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:09.750
<i>May the scarlet kadsuras of Mount 
Afusaka live up to their name</i>

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:09.610
<i>He's snatching up cards while Chihaya-chan's 
busy worrying about the top row.</i>

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.280
<i>Eyelashes...</i>

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.710
<i>By making such drastic changes
to your placement,</i>

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.300
<i>you put pressure on yourself, too...</i>

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.220
<i>along with a sense of adversity and tension.</i>

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:26.390
<i>He's desperate, but it's working.</i>

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:29.040
<i>Just how strong is his 
concentration, anyway?</i>

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.560
<i>He was already good at memorization,</i>

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.880
<i>but he's reformed it into 
something even stronger!</i>

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:36.630
<i>Mashima-senpai...</i>

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.400
<i>How can you...</i>

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.620
<i>How can you pull off something like that?</i>

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.160
<i>Mashima-senpai...</i>

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.400
<i>This is hard.</i>

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.250
<i>It's hard to attack his side.</i>

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.710
<i>I have to persevere.</i>

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:53.370
<i>Don't lose any of the ones on my side.</i>

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.290
<i>Check them over...</i>

00:14:54.290 --> 00:15:02.060
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.380
<i>Check them over...</i>

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.550
<i>This is hard...</i>

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:01.160
<i>It's hard to breathe...</i>

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:10.140
<i>The emotions experienced after 
a long-awaited reunion</i>

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.170
<i>Chihaya-chan faulted!</i>

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.300
<i>Not only that...</i>

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:08.670
<i>It's a semi-double fault!</i>

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.780
<i>"The emotions" on Taichi's side was read,</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.640
<b>Semi-Double Fault</b>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.640
<b>Correct card</b>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.640
<b>Fault</b>

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.280
<i>and she hit "The sight of 
the" on her own side!</i>

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.420
<i>The first mistake! That'll hurt!</i>

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.320
<i>Alas, another autumn has passed in vain</i>

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.880
<i>He avoided sending "Impassioned" 
to make her try to target it,</i>

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.570
<i>but now he's sent her
the last overlapping "Im—" card!</i>

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.420
<i>One of her target cards 
is on her own side now!</i>

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.830
<i>This is hard...</i>

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.890
<i>I didn't know momentum 
could be built this way.</i>

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:46.580
<i>He's using multiple strategies to 
make her focus on her own side.</i>

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.910
<i>If she takes any, they're on her side.</i>

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:52.600
<i>She believes in offensive karuta,
 but he's making her play defensively.</i>

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:56.100
<i>It's hard to breathe...</i>

00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:59.160
<i>Maintain your posture.</i>

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:06.570
<i>Don't close off my chest.</i>

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.610
<i>Raise my eye level.</i>

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.030
Oh... It's you, Taichi.

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:23.710
Huh?

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.210
Uh, yeah, it's me.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:36.340
<i>banish any lingering memories of the past</i>

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:44.840
<i>Impassioned was your promise of salvation</i>

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.770
<i>Their hands...</i>

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:42.720
<i>He got it, just barely!</i>

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:43.760
<i>Right after he sent it!</i>

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.530
<i>He took his time sending that card.</i>

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:51.750
<i>Mashima knows where Ayase 
prefers to put "Impassioned."</i>

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:56.530
<i>Before he even sent that card,
he'd already memorized where it would be!</i>

00:16:58.400 --> 00:16:59.630
Are you okay?

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:00.280
Huh?

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.340
I bumped your finger, right? Are you okay?

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.790
Oh... Yeah, I'm fine.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:08.810
Good.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.000
<i>He's Taichi.</i>

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.330
<i>He's playing like someone I don't know,</i>

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.810
<i>but he's Taichi.</i>

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:35.070
<i>He's Taichi, but he seems like a stranger.</i>

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.450
<i>But he's Taichi.</i>

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.910
<i>He's the guy who's worked so 
hard with me all this time.</i>

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:58.590
<i>His side... my side...</i>

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.090
<i>His side?</i>

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:01.600
<i>My side?</i>

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:14.480
<i>Look for the sound of the cuckoo</i>

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.190
<i>but instead you see a pale 
moon in the dawn sky</i>

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:14.650
<i>"L-Look for the sound"?</i>

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:15.460
<i>She's fast!</i>

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:19.670
<i>He's Taichi. I don't have to be afraid.</i>

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.500
<i>But I don't want to lose.</i>

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:26.150
<i>There's no "his side" or "my side."</i>

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:27.500
<i>Here I come, Taichi!</i>

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:30.590
<i>Chihaya, you idiot! I have a plan!</i>

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:32.750
<i>I won't play along with 
your contest of speed!</i>

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:43.870
<i>Ayase-senpai is looking at Mashima-senpai.</i>

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:47.010
<i>She's looking...</i>

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:49.120
<i>She's looking at him.</i>

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:53.020
<i>Even if it's not out of love or romance...</i>

00:18:54.220 --> 00:19:01.640
<i>The hazed early dawn mist 
over the Kawagiri River</i>

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:58.290
<i>He beat me to a multi-syllable card!</i>

00:18:58.290 --> 00:18:59.540
<i>Better believe it!</i>

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:05.800
<i>Those eyes are looking at Mashima-senpai,
just like he has always wanted...</i>

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.620
Wh-What is it, Kana-chan?

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.810
Desktomu-kun, don't you remember?

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:18.140
When I played against you in 
the Class D final last year...

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.960
I was able to give 120 percent

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:24.260
because I was playing against you.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:28.170
Because I wasn't all worked up 
about playing my own karuta.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:33.520
To this day, that's still the 
best game I've ever played.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.550
Don't you think Chihaya-chan 
and President Mashima

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:48.500
are both at their absolute best
in this match, too?

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.420
Have a good night.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.070
Everyone's out until late tonight.

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:00.670
So, dinner for Chihaya...

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.680
<b>1 new message 

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:07.420
What?!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:15.650
Sender: Chihaya's cell 
Subject: Final round 

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:10.770
I made it to the final for the first time!

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:13.470
I'll do my best in the 
kimono you bought for me!

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:16.490
You should come watch if you have time, Mom!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.310
<i>The last Class A tournament before
the Master and Queen tournament qualifiers</i>

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:24.640
<i>comes down to two high 
schoolers in the final.</i>

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:28.420
<i>I thought they got here on pure momentum, 
but they're not to be taken lightly.</i>

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.460
<i>What are this year's qualifiers 
going to be like?</i>

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.210
Arata...

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:39.760
When did you have the 
most fun playing karuta?

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:56.310
<i>What...</i>

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.020
<i>is this?</i>

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.730
<i>What is it?</i>

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:06.550
<i>Chihaya-chan takes cards,
and Eyelashes picks them up.</i>

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.150
<i>Who will be the one to 
seize the flow in the end?</i>

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.660
<i>Which one?!</i>

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.300
<i>What is this?</i>

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.830
<i>Why did I lose?</i>

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.420
<i>Why...</i>

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.670
<i>Why aren't I the one</i>

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.660
<i>playing against Chihaya right now?</i>

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:30.010
<i>reminds me of the lonely 
dawns after we parted</i>
